{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"876475c3f4d34150934cda3addb2e0d43532bfc08fc91db992b09e97c0d7af62","command":{"allowed_records":[],"directive":"T3-f16cd14a3784f8f8","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"Four compounds (vitexin, baicalin, EGCG and berberine) achieved repigmentation of vitiligo skin lesions via anti-inflammatory effects, the process of which involved the activation of the JAK/STAT pathway","kind":"observe","local_id":"t3_o1","terms":["baicalin in vitiligo","anti-inflammatory mechanism","JAK/STAT pathway"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"Baicalein is a flavonoid extracted from the roots of Scutellaria baicalensis Georgi","kind":"observe","local_id":"t3_o2","terms":["baicalein is a distinct compound from baicalin","source plant"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t3_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t3_c1","object":"anti-inflammatory effects, JAK/STAT activation, in vitiligo","predicate":"reported to achieve repigmentation via","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to promote repigmentation of vitiligo skin lesions through anti-inflammatory effects involving JAK/STAT pathway activation and inhibition of CD8+ T cell-driven autoimmunity."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t3_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t3_c2","object":"baicalin cardiovascular effects or ferroptosis/ACSL4 evidence","predicate":"does not establish","stance":"open","subject":"section d_2334c21c","text":"This section does not address cardiovascular injury, ischemia/reperfusion, ferroptosis or ACSL4; its baicalin content concerns vitiligo only."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b"],"ranges":[["d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b",6860,11632]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"060e9aa029980a5d4aa96975ea41cc7a784561b16b221b64beb003be99560b60","outcome"