n significantly attenuated UVB induced ROS production","kind":"observe","local_id":"t8_o4","terms":["maclurin attenuation of UVB-induced ROS in vitro"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"Previous studies have found that maclurin has pharmacological activities such as anticancer, antioxidant and anti-skin aging","kind":"observe","local_id":"t8_o5","terms":["maclurin reported pharmacological activities"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"CBD increaseed melanin content by binding to CB1 receptor of human epidermal melanocytes.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t8_o6","terms":["CBD melanogenesis via CB1 in melanocytes"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"the molecular mechanism underlying its ability to induce pigmentation is through activation of the p38 signaling pathway","kind":"observe","local_id":"t8_o7","terms":["3,5-diCQM pigmentation mechanism via p38, CREB, cAMP/PKA"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t8_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t8_c1","object":"anti-inflammatory, antioxidant, anti-apoptotic effects (no cardiac context)","predicate":"reported to have","stance":"reported","subject":"cannabidiol (CBD)","text":"CBD is reported to have anti-inflammatory, antioxidant and anti-apoptotic effects, citing Iuvone et al. 2009; the section gives no cardiac, ischemia/reperfusion or ferroptosis data for it."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t8_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t8_c2","object":"reduced intracellular ROS and Nrf2-dependent pathway (no cardiac context)","predicate":"reported to exert antioxidant activity via","stance":"reported","subject":"1,5-dicaffeoylquinic acid","text":"1,5-dicQA is reported to exert antioxidant activity by reducing intracellular ROS and via an Nrf2-dependent pathway, per a previous study; no cardiac or ferroptosis context is given."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t8_o3"],"ki