{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"bbe2e9e1234d703ed22a81e93bcd3fcf5506894388c1ef7ea2d317e99e37f58d","command":{"allowed_records":["257eef540bbc169e8c7813ec3c32f23c9025dcda09386da49faa8a04371a5604","365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","805832a858da54421c2aaa96d5daa665bbecf189579dfcfe58b3b61f1766705e","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T13-cc2e68a969320e46","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"only four natural products (such as Vitexin, baicalin, EGCG and berberine) currently exhibit anti depigmenting pharmacological activity in this model","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o1","terms":["baicalin","anti-depigmenting activity","monobenzone vitiligo model"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"The above mentioned vitiligo models are all inducible and cannot fully replicate the disease characteristics of human vitiligo","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o2","terms":["vitiligo animal models","limits of translation"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"Some natural drugs (such as baicalein, Vitexin, maclurin, etc.) inhibited the damaging effects of H_2O_2-induced oxidative stress on melanocytes","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o3","terms":["baicalein","H2O2 oxidative stress on melanocytes"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"In conclusion, strong evidence that natural products can prevent or treat vitiligo is still lacking.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o4","terms":["strength of evidence","natural products in vitiligo"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"37 natural products can elevate melanin expression by elevating tyrosinase activity in an in vitro melanocyte model","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o5","terms":["melanin induction","tyrosinase","in vitro melanocytes"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"Therefore, it is reasonable to speculate that some of these members contribute to protection against autoimmune destruction.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o6","terms":["speculated protection against autoimmune destruction"]},{"doc_id":"d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b","exact_quote":"their contribution to intervening in autoimmune destruction is similarly unknown","kind":"observe","local_id":"t13_o7","terms":["contribution to autoimmune destruction unknown"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t13_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t13_c1","object":"monobenzone-induced vitiligo model","predicate":"reported to show anti-depigmenting activity in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to be one of four natural products that show anti-depigmenting activity in the monobenzone-induced vitiligo model; the section gives no cardiac context for this."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t13_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t13_c2","object":"H2O2-induced oxidative stress damage to melanocytes","predicate":"reported to inhibit","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalein","text":"Baicalein (not baicalin) is reported to inhibit H2O2-induced oxidative damage to melanocytes; the compound is named separately from baicalin and no cardiac data are given."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t13_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t13_c3","object":"protection against autoimmune destruction","predicate":"speculated to contribute to","stance":"open","subject":"natural products named in the review","text":"The authors speculate that some natural products may protect against autoimmune destruction of melanocytes; this is stated as a hypothesis, not as demonstrated."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t13_o5","t13_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t13_c4","object":"unknown","predicate":"raise melanin expression; contribution to autoimmune destruction is","stance":"open","subject":"37 natural products","text":"The section states that 37 natural products raise melanin via tyrosinase in vitro, but their contribution to autoimmune destruction is unknown."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t13_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t13_c5","object":"still lacking","predicate":"evidence of preventing or treating vitiligo is","stance":"qualified","subject":"natural products","text":"The section concludes that strong evidence that natural products prevent or treat vitiligo is still lacking, and calls for well-designed clinical trials."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t13_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t13_c6","object":"disease characteristics of human vitiligo","predicate":"cannot fully replicate","stance":"qualified","subject":"inducible vitiligo models","text":"The section states that the inducible vitiligo models cannot fully replicate human vitiligo, which makes new drug development harder."},{"based_on":["t13_o1"],"falsifier":"Cardiac I/R studies show baicalin does not reduce lipid peroxidation or ferroptosis markers, or does not act through Nrf2 in heart tissue.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t13_h1","text":"Baicalin's reported Nrf2-linked antioxidant activity may extend to protecting cardiomyocytes from ferroptosis during ischemia/reperfusion."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_2334c21c827f6b7bc5ae2521186c76ffb10084f742cc5447f83253bc2fae9f6b