{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"91f2b3e2c0165b181a99abec1b62c2a2633eb706f949bf7ccab0842b9144f8ed","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T16-ce16fc02aff491f0","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"In addition, mitochondria are key targets of the MIRI mechanism.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o1","terms":["mitochondria as key targets of MIRI mechanism"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Therefore, the VDAC pathway and mPTP may be involved in the mechanism of MIRI.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o2","terms":["VDAC and mPTP possibly involved in MIRI, hedged"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"The opening of the mitochondrial permeability transition pore (mPTP) can lead to elevated mitochondrial ROS production, membrane potential loss, and ATP depletion","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o3","terms":["mPTP opening effects on mitochondria"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Furthermore, the inhibition of GPX-4 activity will promote ROS formation and lipid peroxidation, thereby leading to ferroptosis.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o4","terms":["GPX-4 inhibition and ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Therefore, the inhibition of the System Xc- pathway will reduce intracellular GSH levels, resulting in decreased GPX-4 activity, which will ultimately lead to ferroptosis [30].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o5","terms":["System Xc- inhibition, GSH, GPX-4, ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"SLC7A11 gene silencing with siRNA interference substantially increased the sensitivity of HT-1080 cells to erastin-induced ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o6","terms":["SLC7A11 silencing, HT-1080 cells, erastin"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"When the VDAC-2 or VDAC-3 expression was inhibited by siRNA interference, cells were tolerant to erastin-induced ferroptosis.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o7","terms":["VDAC-2/3 knockdown and erastin-induced ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"However, the overexpression of VDAC-2 or VDAC-3 did not increase cellular sensitivity to erastin.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o8","terms":["VDAC-2/3 overexpression does not sensitize to erastin"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"## 4. The Role of Ferroptosis in MIRI","kind":"observe","local_id":"t16_o9","terms":["section 4 heading on ferroptosis in MIRI, with no body in this section"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o1","t16_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c1","object":"mechanism of myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury (MIRI)","predicate":"may be involved in","stance":"open","subject":"VDAC pathway and mPTP","text":"The section says the VDAC pathway and mPTP may be involved in the MIRI mechanism; this is hedged and no cardiac experimental data are given here."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c2","object":"elevated mitochondrial ROS, membrane potential loss, ATP depletion, cell death","predicate":"can lead to","stance":"reported","subject":"mitochondrial permeability transition pore (mPTP)","text":"Opening of the mPTP is reported to raise mitochondrial ROS, cause membrane potential loss and ATP depletion, and induce cell death; no cardiac-specific data are given in this section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c3","object":"ROS formation, lipid peroxidation, ferroptosis","predicate":"will promote","stance":"reported","subject":"GPX-4 activity inhibition","text":"GPX-4 inhibition is reported to promote ROS formation, lipid peroxidation and ferroptosis; the section gives no compound or cardiac evidence for this."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c4","object":"ferroptosis via reduced GSH and GPX-4","predicate":"will ultimately lead to","stance":"reported","subject":"System Xc- pathway inhibition","text":"Inhibiting System Xc- is reported to reduce intracellular GSH, decrease GPX-4 activity and ultimately lead to ferroptosis, citing reference 30."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c5","object":"silencing increases, overexpression enhances resistance","predicate":"modulates sensitivity to erastin-induced ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"SLC7A11 in HT-1080 cells","text":"In HT-1080 cells, SLC7A11 silencing raised erastin-induced ferroptosis sensitivity, and overexpression reduced it; the evidence is cell-line based and not cardiac."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o7","t16_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c6","object":"erastin-induced ferroptosis (knockdown tolerance; overexpression no sensitization)","predicate":"participate in, per knockdown results","stance":"reported","subject":"VDAC-2 and VDAC-3","text":"In cells, VDAC-2 or VDAC-3 siRNA knockdown conferred tolerance to erastin-induced ferroptosis, but overexpression did not increase sensitivity; this is not cardiac evidence."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t16_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t16_c7","object":"cardioprotective ferroptosis-inhibiting compounds, ACSL4 role in MIRI, baicalin cardiovascular effects","predicate":"does not establish","stance":"open","subject":"section d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","text":"This section names no compound reported to protect the heart from ischemia/reperfusion injury by inhibiting ferroptosis, and does not mention ACSL4 or baicalin; section 4 heading is given but its body is absent here."},{"based_on":["t16_o1","t16_o3"],"falsifier":"Cardiac I/R models in which ferroptosis inhibitors fail to change infarct size or mitochondrial membrane potential, or in which VDAC/mPTP modulation has no effect on ferroptosis markers.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t16_h1","text":"Ferroptosis inhibition may protect against MIRI by preserving mitochondrial membrane potential and limiting mPTP-linked ROS and ATP loss, via VDAC-related pathways."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3"],"ranges":[["d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3",9570,13283]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"a185c3356a19d58b03d18a832dc7335a9b4d0e7018779b4d5b2adb5c552a3937","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["7b692fb8e7e0438127f1a5a8849804780145760c6293fef1977462da608c6b44","a346fec8577d9ca1ededdc7f121dea7a1ad7ca0d27bd79c8f3a304ab44aef96a","2b01f0a7d200be32e498e20578e3edfa2f14311cf01262e18e3809dacbd8c7de","609ef2940385f10d32ef334ebf4fedea75b112c492981669288d62a826c0c958","056d3083644ca6d27026d5cc7f53b4a7cb78467755d6b9c3cba0d14eba288afd","8cf228b81c5a4376a2d383955d79c0f3dd2d20cef41ababa5e2dc459921a8826","dcc640a6aeba00c7789752331f3e160ead72