{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"4418ce7ba24f9a4a43809de42ae1227f7beacb076400e7a5078a9b897caa3ef7","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T17-d1a527de70fbf171","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"MIRI is a phenomenon wherein cardiac function does not improve but worsens immediately after perfusion is restored to the ischemic myocardium.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o1","terms":["definition of myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury (MIRI)"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"As research progresses, ferroptosis has been identified as a form of cell death in MIRI pathogenesis that is closely related to oxidative stress.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o2","terms":["ferroptosis in MIRI","link to oxidative stress"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"At present, it is known to primarily be involved in processes such as oxidative stress, calcium overload, and in inflammatory reactions [42].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o3","terms":["MIRI mechanisms: oxidative stress, calcium overload, inflammation"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"The pathogenic mechanism of MIRI is not fully understood.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o4","terms":["incomplete understanding of MIRI pathogenesis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Deferoxamine is a frequently used iron-chelating agent.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o5","terms":["deferoxamine as iron chelator"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"when performing CABG, the intravenous infusion of deferoxamine 8 h after anesthesia was effective in ameliorating oxygen radical production","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o6","terms":["deferoxamine in CAD patients undergoing CABG, clinical study [45]","reduced oxygen radical production"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"adding a certain concentration of deferoxamine at the early stage of perfusion could effectively attenuate reperfusion-induced free radical generation","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o7","terms":["deferoxamine in isolated rabbit heart perfusion [46]","reduced reperfusion free radical generation"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"At present, peroxidized phosphatidylethanolamine (PEox) has been identified as a predictive biomarker of ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o8","terms":["PEox as ferroptosis biomarker"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"which provided direct evidence for the occurrence of ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes [44]","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o9","terms":["GCIB-SIMS evidence of ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes [44]"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Most current studies investigating the role of ferroptosis in MIRI have mainly focused on endoplasmic reticulum stress (ERS) and ROS production","kind":"observe","local_id":"t17_o10","terms":["focus areas of ferroptosis studies in MIRI","ACSL4 not named"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o5","t17_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c1","object":"CAD patients undergoing CABG (clinical study)","predicate":"reported to protect myocardium from reperfusion injury via reduced oxygen radical production in","stance":"reported","subject":"deferoxamine","text":"Deferoxamine is reported to protect the myocardium from reperfusion injury in CAD patients undergoing CABG by reducing oxygen radical production, with larger benefit when LVEF is reduced."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c2","object":"isolated rabbit hearts (perfusion experiment)","predicate":"reported to attenuate reperfusion-induced free radical generation and give cardioprotection in","stance":"reported","subject":"deferoxamine","text":"In isolated rabbit hearts, deferoxamine added early in perfusion is reported to attenuate reperfusion-induced free radical generation and achieve cardioprotection."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o5","t17_o6","t17_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c3","object":"MIRI cardioprotection","predicate":"mechanism not stated as ferroptosis inhibition in","stance":"qualified","subject":"deferoxamine","text":"Deferoxamine's cardioprotection is reported only through free-radical and oxygen-radical reduction; the section does not state that it inhibits ferroptosis."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c4","object":"oxidative stress in MIRI","predicate":"reported to be a cell death form closely related to","stance":"reported","subject":"ferroptosis","text":"Ferroptosis is reported as a form of cell death in MIRI that is closely related to oxidative stress."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o8","t17_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c5","object":"cardiomyocytes","predicate":"reported to be a predictive biomarker of, and direct evidence for, ferroptosis in","stance":"reported","subject":"PEox and GCIB-SIMS","text":"PEox is reported as a predictive biomarker of ferroptosis, and GCIB-SIMS is reported to give direct evidence of ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o3","t17_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c6","object":"oxidative stress, calcium overload, inflammation","predicate":"reported as not fully understood, mainly involving","stance":"qualified","subject":"MIRI pathogenesis","text":"MIRI pathogenesis is reported as not fully understood, mainly involving oxidative stress, calcium overload and inflammatory reactions."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t17_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t17_c7","object":"ERS, ROS, GPX-4, autophagy-dependent ferroptotic pathway","predicate":"mainly focus on, with ACSL4 not named among","stance":"open","subject":"ferroptosis studies in MIRI","text":"The section's listed ferroptosis focus areas in MIRI are ERS, ROS production, GPX-4 and the autophagy-dependent ferroptotic pathway; ACSL4 is not named."},{"based_on":["t17_o5","t17_o7"],"falsifier":"Cited studies [45] and [46] measure no ferroptosis markers (e.g., PEox, GPX-4, lipid peroxidation) and attribute benefit only to radical reduction.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t17_h1","text":"Deferoxamine's cardioprotection in these works may act partly through ferroptosis suppression, since it is an iron chelator and ferroptosis is iron-dependent."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3"],"ranges":[["d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3",13283,16011]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"3a3e2cacda5232a98d00db93a0bc130d974db044e20a511983cc6d93e88caf86","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["5fc52af9291cb9777f859cc291604d322e0d3bbd59b0db81290391371f4e31f0","e0c187e758bec4387de42de5bff65aeb23a5967b871972d32c349bf7473ee897","cb0ad2