{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"6cd8b229bffaad08972def46cb68c73f8eff285ec9b4ef936e3336844f29d6a7","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T19-00bbbf013114a8c6","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Another study found that liproxstatin-1 inhibited ferroptosis by increasing GPX-4 levels, which decreased ROS levels and thus alleviated MIRI [65].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o1","terms":["liproxstatin-1","GPX-4","ferroptosis","MIRI"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Liproxstatin-1 has been shown to significantly inhibit ferroptosis and attenuate MIRI by reducing the accumulation of ROS from lipid peroxidation","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o2","terms":["liproxstatin-1","lipid peroxidation","ROS","MIRI"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"there is evidence showing that the specific overexpression of GPX-4 in mitochondria attenuates cardiac dysfunction in MIRI [61]","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o3","terms":["GPX-4 overexpression","mitochondria","cardiac dysfunction","MIRI"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"the levels of iron and malondialdehyde (MDA) in reperfused rat hearts gradually increased with increasing reperfusion time","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o4","terms":["iron","MDA","reperfused rat hearts","reperfusion time"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Following the overexpression of SIRT-1, the cardiomyocytes showed a significant improvement in the extent of ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o5","terms":["SIRT-1","cardiomyocytes","ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"the regulation of ROS may be related to the SIRT-1/p53/SLC7A11 signaling pathway [71].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o6","terms":["SIRT-1/p53/SLC7A11","ROS","hypothesized mechanism"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"During MIRI, iron accumulates in cardiomyocytes around the myocardial scar, and excess iron leads to cardiomyocyte death","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o7","terms":["iron","cardiomyocyte death","MIRI"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"The indirect or direct inactivation of GPX-4 is the classic induction mechanism of ferroptosis.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o8","terms":["GPX-4 inactivation","ferroptosis induction"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"The increase in ROS leads to lipid peroxidation and ferroptosis, which can be inhibited by the iron chelator deferoxamine [69].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o9","terms":["deferoxamine","iron chelator","ROS","ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"In turn, the large production of ROS and ferroptosis are important mechanisms leading to MIRI [63, 64].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o10","terms":["ROS","ferroptosis","MIRI pathogenesis"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Increased expression of antioxidant enzymes protects tissues from oxidative stress and produces cardioprotection after myocardial reperfusion [66].","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o11","terms":["antioxidant enzymes","cardioprotection","reperfusion"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Therefore, in MIRI, increasing GPX-4 expression can inhibit ferroptosis and attenuate the negative effects of MIRI.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o12","terms":["GPX-4 expression","ferroptosis","MIRI"]},{"doc_id":"d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3","exact_quote":"Ferroptosis is highly correlated with cardiomyocyte death.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t19_o13","terms":["ferroptosis","cardiomyocyte death"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o1","t19_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c1","object":"GPX-4 increase and ROS reduction","predicate":"reported to inhibit ferroptosis and alleviate MIRI via","stance":"reported","subject":"liproxstatin-1","text":"Liproxstatin-1 is reported to inhibit ferroptosis and alleviate MIRI by increasing GPX-4 levels and reducing ROS, based on cited studies; no sample size or model is given in the section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c2","object":"cardiac dysfunction in MIRI","predicate":"reported to attenuate","stance":"reported","subject":"mitochondrial GPX-4 overexpression","text":"Specific mitochondrial overexpression of GPX-4 is reported to attenuate cardiac dysfunction in MIRI, citing one study."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c3","object":"reperfusion time","predicate":"reported iron and MDA increase with","stance":"reported","subject":"reperfused rat hearts","text":"In reperfused rat hearts, iron and MDA levels are reported to rise gradually with reperfusion time, citing a previous study."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c4","object":"ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes in MIRI models","predicate":"reported to improve","stance":"reported","subject":"SIRT-1 overexpression","text":"SIRT-1 overexpression is reported to improve ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes in MIRI in vivo and in vitro models."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c5","object":"ROS regulation in MIRI ferroptosis","predicate":"may be related to","stance":"open","subject":"SIRT-1/p53/SLC7A11 pathway","text":"A SIRT-1/p53/SLC7A11 pathway is proposed as possibly linking ROS regulation to MIRI ferroptosis; the section frames this as tentative ('may be related')."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c6","object":"ROS-driven lipid peroxidation and ferroptosis","predicate":"reported to inhibit","stance":"reported","subject":"deferoxamine","text":"Deferoxamine, an iron chelator, is reported to inhibit ROS-driven lipid peroxidation and ferroptosis; this is stated generally, not specifically for the heart."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c7","object":"MIRI","predicate":"reported as mechanisms leading to","stance":"reported","subject":"ROS and ferroptosis","text":"Large ROS production and ferroptosis are reported as important mechanisms leading to MIRI, citing two studies."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o11"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c8","object":"cardioprotection after myocardial reperfusion","predicate":"reported to produce","stance":"reported","subject":"antioxidant enzymes","text":"Increased antioxidant enzyme expression is reported to protect tissues from oxidative stress and produce cardioprotection after myocardial reperfusion."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o7","t19_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c9","object":"cardiomyocyte death in MIRI","predicate":"reported to cause","stance":"reported","subject":"iron and ferroptosis","text":"During MIRI, iron accumulates around the myocardial scar and excess iron is reported to cause cardiomyocyte death; ferroptosis is described as highly correlated with cardiomyocyte death."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c10","object":"ferroptosis","predicate":"is the classic induction mechanism of","stance":"reported","subject":"GPX-4 inactivation","text":"Inactivation of GPX-4, directly or indirectly, is stated as the classic induction mechanism of ferroptosis; this general statement is not specific to the heart."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t19_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t19_c11","object":"ferroptosis and attenuate MIRI effects","predicate":"reported to inhibit","stance":"reported","subject":"GPX-4 expression","text":"Increasing GPX-4 expression is concluded to inhibit ferroptosis and attenuate negative effects of MIRI; this conclusion rests on the cited studies summarized in the section."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3"],"ranges":[["d_a4ddf8ee6d280b8bf83b9085b69d8b452885166ab36aa6da396cd4b3b96a32e3",20036,25928]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"076621ebb2e6183a8c1cdccb0d1e4a39b88daaad99addde38ebde27293237e35","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["fbabd6969f766c63fb51c0167befc532aef347fe38458c8753dc3fb6f9815ca2","756d27a735214c6fa96fa01ace325043212163d512fb3224ae49f7fb7b449f6b","d607dd2d31044d4c40da42e4c3adac5aee698935d40fa58869b3cc2f779329c0","74e477eb9e237e79a5cf707cc28d60b8d2681625edf17d91bccf225c57c5ae80","c8d47a74b00b77781d1b75e332155077693b9c821bbee1b82b3237044e5212e5","d15872ad8ddca0f9cb3d211637e823fb6cd0233e1fa36eb4ec26970e7856755f","d699dd1ab755d02be52e2173b5ad98b68000146872ae5ab5c36008b17f4568a6","cebfe7117e142b438860b664a610149f326fee620330f85b7bd7c205741da4c3","0c0e584d82f85601160e547b87e6f6271076d89eb527937fc43e17da8f95de00","0a32f32fc81a13d452c6cd