{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"3ec6c9dc6ae3f079052dcb789cb8203f520019781e4f01d75bd42a002ab3617d","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T23-517c7059f76d1b15","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"this could also trigger profound myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury such as myocardial cell death","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o1","terms":["PCI reperfusion triggers myocardial I/R injury","AMI background"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Emerging evidence indicated that ferroptosis is implicated in myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury (Park et al., 2019).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o2","terms":["ferroptosis in myocardial I/R injury","cited background"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Previous studies indicate that ACSL4 is essential for ferroptosis induction, and ACSL4 inhibition can prevent ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o3","terms":["ACSL4 role in ferroptosis","ACSL4 inhibition"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"GPX4 is considered as the primary enzyme that inhibits ferroptosis by converting lipid hydroperoxides into nontoxic lipid alcohols","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o4","terms":["GPX4 as ferroptosis inhibitor","lipid peroxide repair"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin has also been demonstrated to decrease ACSL4 expression, leading to an anti-fibrotic effect (Wu et al., 2018).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o5","terms":["baicalin reduces ACSL4 expression","anti-fibrotic effect"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The protective effects of baicalin on myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury have been documented in previous studies","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o6","terms":["baicalin cardioprotection in I/R, cited"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin evidently improved left ventricle hemodynamic parameters, myocardial infarction area, and cell apoptosis relative I/R model controls","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o7","terms":["baicalin in I/R model: hemodynamics, infarct area, apoptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"the cell activity and function were restored in hypoxia-reoxygenation–challenged cardiac microvascular endothelial cells after baicalin treatment","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o8","terms":["baicalin in hypoxia-reoxygenation cardiac endothelial cells"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The excessive ROS production induced by oxygen–glucose deprivation/reperfusion was suppressed by baicalin intervention","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o9","terms":["baicalin suppresses ROS in OGD/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"However, whether baicalin exerts protective effects against myocardial ischemia-reperfusion damage via ferroptosis resistance is not understood.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o10","terms":["baicalin anti-ferroptosis effect in I/R unknown"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Thus, in the current study, we investigated the anti-ferroptosis effect of baicalin on myocardial I/R injury","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o11","terms":["study aim, rat I/R and H9c2 OGD/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"It has been reported that baicalin reduced MDA level and enhanced glutathione peroxidase and SOD activities in the brain cortex of mice","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o12","terms":["baicalin antioxidant effects in brain injury (non-cardiac)"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"TfR1 and ferritinophagy are identified as important regulators of iron accumulation","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o13","terms":["iron regulators in ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Diltiazem (20 mg/kg), a specific L-type calcium channel blocker, was selected as positive control based on previous studies","kind":"observe","local_id":"t23_o14","terms":["diltiazem as positive control in I/R study"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c1","object":"myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury","predicate":"is implicated in","stance":"reported","subject":"ferroptosis","text":"Ferroptosis is reported to be implicated in myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury, citing Park et al. 2019; no mechanism or data are given in this section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c2","object":"ferroptosis","predicate":"is essential for ferroptosis induction; inhibition prevents","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"Cited previous studies indicate ACSL4 is essential for ferroptosis induction and that ACSL4 inhibition prevents ferroptosis; this is stated as background, not as I/R-specific data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c3","object":"ferroptosis via lipid hydroperoxide conversion","predicate":"is the primary enzyme that inhibits","stance":"reported","subject":"GPX4","text":"GPX4 is described as the primary enzyme inhibiting ferroptosis by converting lipid hydroperoxides into nontoxic lipid alcohols; this is background, not a compound test."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c4","object":"myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury","predicate":"can trigger","stance":"reported","subject":"PCI reperfusion","text":"Reperfusion after PCI in acute myocardial infarction is said to trigger myocardial I/R injury, including cell death and deterioration of cardiac function (Liang et al., 2017)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c5","object":"anti-fibrotic effect","predicate":"decreases ACSL4 expression, leading to","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to decrease ACSL4 expression, producing an anti-fibrotic effect (Wu et al., 2018); the tissue context of this fibrosis finding is not stated in the section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c6","object":"myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury","predicate":"has documented protective effects on","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Protective effects of baicalin on myocardial I/R injury are said to be documented in previous studies (Wang 2013; Bai 2019; Luan 2019); the section gives no details beyond these citations."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c7","object":"left ventricle hemodynamics, infarct area and apoptosis in I/R model","predicate":"improved","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In an I/R model, baicalin is reported (Luan et al., 2019) to improve left ventricle hemodynamics, reduce myocardial infarction area and reduce cell apoptosis versus I/R controls."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c8","object":"hypoxia-reoxygenation-challenged cardiac microvascular endothelial cells","predicate":"restored cell activity and function in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In hypoxia-reoxygenation-challenged cardiac microvascular endothelial cells, baicalin is reported (Bai et al., 2019) to restore cell activity and function."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c9","object":"excessive ROS production induced by OGD/R","predicate":"suppresses","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported (Wang G. et al., 2018) to suppress excessive ROS production induced by oxygen-glucose deprivation/reperfusion; the section does not state the cell type."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c10","object":"ferroptosis resistance","predicate":"is not known to protect against I/R via","stance":"open","subject":"baicalin","text":"The section states it is not understood whether baicalin protects against myocardial I/R damage via ferroptosis resistance."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o11"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c11","object":"baicalin anti-ferroptosis effect on myocardial I/R injury","predicate":"aim to investigate, results not shown","stance":"open","subject":"this study's experiments","text":"The section states an aim to test baicalin's anti-ferroptosis effect in rat I/R and OGD/R H9c2 cells; no results for these experiments appear in this section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o12"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c12","object":"brain cortex after traumatic brain injury in mice","predicate":"reduced MDA and enhanced GPx and SOD in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to reduce MDA and raise glutathione peroxidase and SOD activity in brain cortex of mice after traumatic brain injury; this is non-cardiac evidence."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c13","object":"iron accumulation in ferroptosis","predicate":"are important regulators of","stance":"reported","subject":"TfR1 and ferritinophagy","text":"TfR1 and ferritinophagy are described as important regulators of iron accumulation for ferroptosis; NCOA4 mediates ferritinophagy. Background only."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t23_o14"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t23_c14","object":"myocardial I/R study","predicate":"is used as positive control in","stance":"reported","subject":"diltiazem","text":"Diltiazem (20 mg/kg), an L-type calcium channel blocker, is used as positive control in the I/R study; it is not presented as a ferroptosis inhibitor."},{"based_on":["t23_o5","t23_o10","t23_o3"],"falsifier":"Rat I/R or H9c2 OGD/R experiments show no change in ferroptosis markers or ACSL4 level with baicalin, or ACSL4 inhibition does not alter baicalin's protection.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t23_h1","text":"Baicalin protects against myocardial I/R injury partly by inhibiting ACSL4-linked ferroptosis, consistent with its reported ACSL4-lowering effect."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de"],"ranges":[["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de",2280,7031]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"0436181a3470463d8fcafef0cf7b4d16631a83a9bab5fb15b1b730ae82c20799","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["0002b0370ce45e3fc61556fd438de05a5d5f601284017bd2babb6fe8a8fb9451","b602d4ade9efbfd7109f951553b2f220751b70889711623dcf68af1723d6bacc","4676802df183c105b38eb6574caead6d0f1cc195618e26c2c11fef21a713ce29","811fc5314fb8ba659c213860efb9eef54205ab44720e99270b377e5138563ff8","9a59d3d135bfe10fe44fa7d7d34bdcc1f5ac20c079d66b8c2b1c826176ae76c2","d284e3a9e38348bca4241954b74fff28da34bf0a2004f187e55dac7f1a5d7be2","8134b816bfb39