{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"c6c9ce30fb9aac611ee6bf16a6b19ffa23dbc10f5950d50230c1f432ac848e10","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T25-98b7f8e4f874cbff","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"To estimate the role of baicalin on myocardial I/R injury, rats were pretreated with baicalin for 6 days prior to I/R injury (Figure 1A).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o1","terms":["baicalin in vivo pretreatment design, rat myocardial I/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"the infarct size was significantly higher in the I/R group than in the control group (I/R: 34.96% vs. control: 0.7767%)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o2","terms":["infarct size in I/R versus control rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"pretreatment of baicalin and diltiazem decreased the ST segment elevation and infarct size (BA-100: 21.80%, BA-200: 16.13%, DI-20: 21.78% vs. I/R)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o3","terms":["baicalin and diltiazem reduce ST elevation and infarct size"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Nonetheless, recovery of CF (BA-100: 8.317 ml/min, BA-200: 9.882 ml/min, DI-20: 11.46 ml/min vs. I/R)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o4","terms":["baicalin effect on coronary flow after I/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"A certain degree of attenuation was observed in diltiazem and low-dose baicalin group, and more evident alleviation was noticed in high-dose baicalin group","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o5","terms":["dose-related histological attenuation of myocardial injury by baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Collectively, these data suggested that baicalin protected rats from myocardial I/R injury.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o6","terms":["authors' conclusion on baicalin cardioprotection in rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin Prevents Myocardial Ischemia/Reperfusion-Induced Ferroptosis in Rats","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o7","terms":["section heading on ferroptosis; no ferroptosis data follow in this section"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin interventions (25, 50, 100 μM) were applied 24 h prior to the onset of OGD.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o8","terms":["in vitro baicalin pretreatment concentrations before OGD in H9c2 cells"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The ACSL4 overexpression vectors and corresponding negative controls were synthesized by Shanghai Genechem Co., Ltd.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o9","terms":["ACSL4 overexpression construct in H9c2 cells; no ACSL4 outcome reported here"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The OGD/R model was established as described previously (Wu et al., 2013).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o10","terms":["OGD/R model in H9c2 cells, cited method"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"after 40 min of ligation, evident ST segment elevation was detected in I/R group relative to control animals","kind":"observe","local_id":"t25_o11","terms":["ST elevation confirming I/R model in rats"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o1","t25_o2","t25_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c1","object":"rat myocardial I/R injury (pretreatment model)","predicate":"reduces infarct size and ST elevation in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In rats, baicalin pretreatment (6 days) lowered ST elevation and infarct size after myocardial I/R; infarct size was 16.13-21.80% versus 34.96% in I/R controls."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o4"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c2","object":"I/R-injured rat hearts","predicate":"partly restores coronary flow and LVSP in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin partly restored coronary flow and left ventricular systolic pressure after I/R in rats; dP/dt was not affected by I/R in the reported data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c3","object":"rat myocardium","predicate":"reportedly attenuates morphological I/R injury, dose-related, in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Histology reportedly shows attenuated I/R myocardial injury with baicalin, more marked at the high dose; this is qualitative and not graded in the section."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c4","object":"myocardial I/R injury in rats","predicate":"is concluded to protect against","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"The authors conclude baicalin protected rats from myocardial I/R injury; the conclusion rests on ECG, infarct, hemodynamic and histology readouts from one rat model."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c5","object":"rat I/R model","predicate":"serves as comparator with similar reduction of infarct size in","stance":"reported","subject":"diltiazem","text":"Diltiazem served as a comparator and gave similar reductions in ST elevation and infarct size as baicalin in this model."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c6","object":"myocardial I/R (no data in section)","predicate":"heading asserts prevention of ferroptosis in","stance":"open","subject":"baicalin","text":"The section's heading says baicalin prevents I/R-induced ferroptosis, but no ferroptosis measurement appears in the excerpt, so this claim is left open here."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o8","t25_o10"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c7","object":"25, 50, 100 μM in H9c2 cells","predicate":"applied in vitro before OGD/R at","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In H9c2 cells, baicalin (25, 50, 100 μM) was applied 24 h before OGD/R; the section gives the design only, not outcomes for ACSL4 or ferroptosis."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t25_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t25_c8","object":"I/R or ferroptosis","predicate":"is overexpressed in H9c2 cells with unreported functional effect in","stance":"open","subject":"ACSL4","text":"ACSL4 overexpression vectors were built and used in H9c2 cells, but the section reports no effect of ACSL4 on I/R or ferroptosis, so its role is left open."},{"based_on":["t25_o8","t25_o9"],"falsifier":"ACSL4 overexpression fails to reduce baicalin's protective effect on viability or ferroptosis markers in OGD/R H9c2 cells","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t25_h1","text":"Baicalin protects H9c2 cells from OGD/R partly by suppressing ACSL4-dependent ferroptosis, so ACSL4 overexpression should blunt that protection."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de"],"ranges":[["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de",12466,17685]],