{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"873d59998c3598de61ad5d2fe4631be537647f4baf227d8c5d620b16a153d854","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T26-8b3d43e12ee94bf8","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"ACSL4 is an essential enzyme that synthesizes polyunsaturated fatty acid containing phospholipids, the primary substrates for lipid peroxidation","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o1","terms":["ACSL4 role as enzyme producing PUFA phospholipid substrates for lipid peroxidation"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"the ACSL4 expression (I/R: 4.411 vs. control: 1.000) was dramatically upregulated","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o2","terms":["ACSL4 expression up in myocardial I/R rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"GPX4 expression (I/R: 0.1480 vs. control: 0.9980) downregulated in I/R group","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o3","terms":["GPX4 expression down in myocardial I/R rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Nonetheless, baicalin and diltiazem successfully reduced ROS","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o4","terms":["baicalin and diltiazem reduce ROS in I/R rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"suggesting the inhibition effect of baicalin and diltiazem on ROS production and lipid peroxidation in myocardial I/R model rats","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o5","terms":["authors' interpretation of baicalin and diltiazem effect on ROS and lipid peroxidation"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"These findings demonstrate that baicalin and diltiazem reduce the intracellular iron levels through mediating iron uptake and the autophagic degradation of ferritin","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o6","terms":["proposed mechanism: iron uptake and ferritin autophagic degradation"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"which was remarkably alleviated by baicalin or diltiazem treatment","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o7","terms":["baicalin lowers Fe2+ accumulation in I/R rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Overall, these results indicate the activation of NCOA4-medicated ferritinophagy following I/R.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o8","terms":["NCOA4 ferritinophagy activation after I/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"indicating that baicalin provided myocardial protection against ischemia/reperfusion in vitro","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o9","terms":["in vitro cardioprotection claim, H9c2 OGD/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"which were reversed by baicalin treatment (BA-25: 68.10%, BA-50: 74.26%, BA-100: 85.80% vs. OGD/R)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o10","terms":["baicalin restores H9c2 viability after OGD/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Given lipid peroxidation by excessive intracellular ROS is the key event during ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o12","terms":["framing of lipid peroxidation as key ferroptosis event"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"GPX4 is the essential phospholipid peroxidase responsible for reducing lipid peroxides","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o14","terms":["GPX4 role in reducing lipid peroxides"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"promoted SOD activity (BA-100: 51.39 U/g, BA-200: 80.78 U/g, DI-20: 77.30 U/g vs. I/R) and GPX4 expression","kind":"observe","local_id":"t26_o18","terms":["baicalin raises SOD and GPX4 versus I/R"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o4","t26_o5","t26_o18"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c1","object":"myocardial I/R model rats (in vivo)","predicate":"reported to inhibit ROS production and lipid peroxidation in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In myocardial I/R rats, baicalin (BA-100, BA-200) is reported to reduce ROS, MDA and ACSL4 and to raise SOD and GPX4, taken as inhibition of ROS production and lipid peroxidation."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o7","t26_o8","t26_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c2","object":"iron uptake and NCOA4-mediated ferritinophagy in I/R rats","predicate":"reported to reduce iron accumulation via","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to lower Fe2+ in I/R rat hearts and reverse TfR1, FTH1, NCOA4 and LC3-II/I changes, with the authors proposing iron uptake and ferritin autophagic degradation as the mechanism."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o10","t26_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c3","object":"OGD/R-challenged H9c2 cardiomyocyte-like cells (in vitro)","predicate":"reported to improve viability of","stance":"qualified","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to raise viability of H9c2 cells after OGD/R, with no cytotoxicity up to the highest tested non-toxic dose; the section frames this as in vitro protection only."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o1","t26_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c4","object":"myocardial I/R injury (rat model)","predicate":"reported to promote lipid peroxidation in","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"ACSL4 is reported to be upregulated in I/R hearts and lowered by baicalin; the section describes ACSL4 as an enzyme that makes PUFA phospholipids, the substrates of lipid peroxidation."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o3","t26_o14","t26_o18"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c5","object":"myocardial I/R injury (rat model)","predicate":"reported to protect against lipid peroxidation in","stance":"reported","subject":"GPX4","text":"GPX4 is reported to be downregulated in I/R hearts and raised by baicalin; GPX4 is described as the phospholipid peroxidase that reduces lipid peroxides."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t26_o12","t26_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t26_c6","object":"marker changes in this section alone","predicate":"not established by","stance":"open","subject":"ferroptosis attribution of baicalin effects","text":"The section does not show a ferroptosis-specific inhibitor control or a causal test linking the observed marker changes to ferroptosis; the attribution rests on marker correlations."},{"based_on":["t26_o4","t26_o6","t26_o18"],"falsifier":"A ferroptosis inhibitor or ACSL4 knockdown in the same I/R or OGD/R models abolishes baicalin's protection, or baicalin's protection persists when ferroptosis markers are not changed.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t26_h1","text":"Baicalin protects the ischemic myocardium by suppressing ferroptosis, lowering ROS and ACSL4 and iron/ferritinophagy while restoring GPX4."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de"],"ranges":[["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1