","exact_quote":"GPX4 expression (OGD/R: 0.1880 vs. blank: 1.034; BA-25: 0.3280, BA-50: 0.4820, BA-100: 0.7020 vs. OGD/R)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o4","terms":["GPX4 expression reduced by OGD/R and restored by baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"ACSL4 expression (OGD/R: 4.268 vs. blank: 1.000; BA-25: 2.690, BA-50: 2.174, BA-100: 1.322 vs. OGD/R)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o5","terms":["ACSL4 expression raised by OGD/R and lowered by baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"baicalin ameliorated OGD/R-induced increase of MDA content","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o6","terms":["MDA lipid peroxidation marker reduced by baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The above results suggest that baicalin attenuates OGD/R-induced ROS production and lipid peroxidation in cardiomyocytes.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o7","terms":["authors' summary of ROS and lipid peroxidation effects"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Iron assay reveals that baicalin efficiently protected cardiomyocytes from OGD/R-induced Fe^2+ deposition","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o8","terms":["baicalin reduces Fe2+ accumulation after OGD/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"exhibited lower FTH1 (OGD/R: 0.1880 vs. blank: 1.000) and NCOA4 (OGD/R: 0.1940 vs. blank: 1.000) levels","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o9","terms":["FTH1 and NCOA4 lowered by OGD/R, ferritinophagy markers"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"baicalin treatment suppressed OGD/R-induced GFP-LC3 puncta formation in H9c2 cells","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o10","terms":["baicalin suppresses autophagosome puncta"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"These findings indicate that deactivated TfR1 signal and ferritinophagy are associated with the reduction of iron accumulation following baicalin treatment.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o11","terms":["association of TfR1 and ferritinophagy with iron reduction"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"lentivirus overexpressing ACSL4 was transfected in cardiomyocytes","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o12","terms":["ACSL4 overexpression model design"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"ACSL4 overexpression hampered baicalin-induced protective effect on ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o13","terms":["ACSL4 overexpression blunts baicalin protection"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"cell survival (OGD/R + BA-100 + ACSL4-OE: 39.73% vs. OGD/R + BA-100)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o14","terms":["survival reduced by ACSL4-OE under baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"baicalin improved cell viability (OGD/R: 58.13% vs. blank: 100.0%; OGD/R + BA-100: 86.42% vs. OGD/R)","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o15","terms":["viability improved by baicalin at 100"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The results demonstrated that baicalin exerts a profound ameliorative effect against myocardial ischemia-reperfusion injury in vitro via ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis resistance.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o16","terms":["authors' conclusion, in vitro, ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"the protein level of ACSL4 in cardiomyocytes was markedly upregulated, suggesting successful lentiviral packaging and cell infection","kind":"observe","local_id":"t27_o17","terms":["ACSL4-OE verified by protein level"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t27_o1","t27_o2","t27_o3","t27_o4","t27_o6","t27_o7"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t27_c1","object":"ROS, MDA and lipid peroxidation; restores SOD and GPX4 in H9c2 OGD/R","predicate":"reported to attenuate","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In OGD/R-treated H9c2 cells, baicalin at 25/50/100 lowered ROS and MDA and restored SOD and GPX4 in a dose-related pattern, in vitro. Section gives no in vivo data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t27_o5"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t27_c2","object":"baicalin in H9c2 cells","predicate":"reported to be raised by OGD/R and lowered by","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"OGD/R raised ACSL4 protein expression in H9c2 cells and baicalin lowered it in a dose-related pattern, in vitro."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t27_o8","t27_o9","t27_o10","t27_o11"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t27_c3","object":"TfR1 and ferritinophagy (NCOA4, FTH1, LC3)","predicate":"reported to reduce, linked by association to","stance":"qualified","subject":"baicalin and iron accumulation","text":"Baicalin reduced Fe2+ deposition in OGD/R cardiomyocytes. The section links this to TfR1 and NCOA4-linked ferritinophagy only as an association, not as demonstrated mechanism."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t27_o12","t27_o13","t27_o14","t27_o17"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t27_c4","object":"baicalin on ferroptosis markers, GPX4 and survival","predicate":"reported to hamper the protective effect of","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4 overexpression","text":"Lentiviral ACSL4 overexpression reduced the protective effect of baicalin on GPX4, ferroptosis markers and cell survival in OGD/R H9c2 cells."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t27_o16","t27_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t27_c5","object":"ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis resistance (in vitro)","predicate":"concluded to ameliorate myocardial I/R injury via","stance":"qualified","subject":"baicalin, ACSL4 and ferroptosis","text":"Authors conclude baicalin ameliorates myocardial ischemia-reperfusion injury via ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis resistance, but the evidence cited is H9c2 OGD/R in vitro only."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t27_o16","t27_o15"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t27_c6","object":"in vitro H9c2 OGD/R experiments","predicate":"reports only","stance":"confirmed","subject":"section d_d3012628","text":"This section reports only in vitro H9c2 OGD/R experiments; it contains no in vivo ischemia-reperfusion data."},{"based_on":["t27_o5","t27_o13","t27_o14"],"falsifier":"Baicalin protects OGD/R cells equally well when ACSL4 is overexpressed, or ACSL4 overexpression alone does not alter ferroptosis markers.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t27_h1","text":"Baicalin's anti-ferroptotic protection in OGD/R cardiomyocytes depends on suppressing ACSL4 signaling."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de"],"ranges":[["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de",22697,26522]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"84cfa0bd098a1c5751c8e88aad2dc2f37520674bb03171df14481c5e0fe54c65","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":["0adc4dac926a0d37fd83c08a9f61c61a5e0b6ec0d583b3913f963cf77b5fafe0","240331d308367a2fe646eb2bdb92e519c074460277016cbd72d674c72f622bc7","3873a9a20ee26bfb334eb628954754ce573d8cee2eca41516d7ecbef370c4abc","f26edbe912150175b145d9f3b5f6522af80efca944f720e11a71e15cd1fcfc20","ad45e9a9a8a9d2121605cbd58e50c1f7afe3627fc0b49a237120004f23b74191","0697569dd74b6ea28ec7a6853715689b93e45abfdbf85e1cac37d3dfb317060d","2bf0420973a898f7cf06466cdf9b1b0172af16db5a84e8f8784223250de5d21e","89b72138454005ce9b538bee1a5a3ab4af4851d92912acbcf29b73e131a8fd16","c16a2d241d77034a9e9cad5ee14bc661e0e6192bb677421a2888493ff36b3150","eeb7065def77d3f07acdd3c8b817ca7174a5feebf090b76bd5bc885acaa3c659","57c199b30f648d8928af5455bca9f3cfa7cca3d33d95e7466c0f7055ee1f0e60","93978871047cc7f052b01a62a9d7299ecd