{"body":{"actor":"w1","audit_root":"fb9e63e1d5b9e74be219f5c70f1dabf4d7d17a968f61df4b19922686bdc9021a","command":{"allowed_records":["365ae9fb0cc44e725fa0d2de0689fec700d542b00dcf815a3dcd3dec48fe3889","4a7b9b4b679f4a3e457033edb67d814162543a07bbd6607182b84c552168225f","68d496f719eefdeadd68cc8fa1c507aa91d6e156b39c7b8e4266c9ceaf46c5ef","69ae6f64ae891c52f8ae1941cf20ce71cb78926c6b047390234a4a06e8c520b0","6f0ff3bf9ad296c5661b98fe021f26761a38e5bbf05983577bf7b3322e76eb77","72bb7299aeed4327bb9a52d6503efcb56be03d734738368149981ecf6912dc95","9026b2ce369c12781d95960bd95ed7f8fe3745adfa12204c62340bd8d77344c7","a400583ce667ce35482f11198679bfb202abd3949671e75fd709db3195831a0c","a84be80a6986ad7f7b387ffa2dce2ef2d38f4cf0ec25289700d894594af2c536","c1c7d8e99994e3cc3629519b9ce5a5feb3379830cbf730f10f1f90f245e9d808","c473d66009fc579f4bd443ed3238a310b97d74bfce00047cff8ddd8350853d69","dcb10951c982480fbffb7a64236be2e7e6f6183f0750f14a98bcbc56c9c06d95"],"directive":"T28-9cf56aad6de4825b","kind":"submit","lines":[{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin is an active compound that has cardioprotection effect against ischemia/reperfusion (I/R) injury (Luan et al., 2019).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o1","terms":["baicalin cardioprotection against I/R injury, cited to Luan 2019"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin protected cardiac microvascular endothelial cells in myocardial I/R rats by mediating the PI3K/AKT/eNOS pathway (Bai et al., 2019).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o2","terms":["PI3K/AKT/eNOS mechanism, endothelial cells, I/R rats"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The infarct-limiting effects of baicalin in myocardial I/R damage are associated with the inhibition of mitochondrial damage-mediated apoptosis (Wang et al., 2013).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o3","terms":["infarct limitation, mitochondrial apoptosis inhibition, Wang 2013"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"by activating PI3K/AKT, but inhibiting NF-κB and JAK/STAT pathway","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o4","terms":["PI3K/AKT activation, NF-kB and JAK/STAT inhibition, apoptosis and inflammation in I/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Our preliminary study suggests that baicalin could suppress myocardial I/R-triggered ferroptosis.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o5","terms":["baicalin anti-ferroptosis, preliminary study, stated as suggestion"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Interestingly, ACSL4 overexpression transfection blocked baicalin-generated protective effects in cardiomyocytes.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o6","terms":["ACSL4 overexpression blocks baicalin protection in cardiomyocytes"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"We found that baicalin improved ST segment elevation, hemodynamic parameters, infarct area, and histopathological changes in rats exposed to myocardial I/R surgery.","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o7","terms":["in vivo rat I/R functional and infarct outcomes with baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"treatment with baicalin attenuated OGD/R-induced ferroptosis","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o8","terms":["in vitro OGD/R ferroptosis attenuated by baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The inhibition of ferroptosis applying ferroptosis inhibitor ferrostatin-1 resulted in substantial improvements in infarct size and left ventricular systolic function","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o9","terms":["ferrostatin-1 benefit on infarct size and LV function, cited Li W. 2019"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"myocardial I/R challenge or OGD/R treatment promoted ROS-induced lipid peroxidation and caused evident iron accumulation by activating TfR1 signaling and NCOA4-medicated ferritinophagy","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o10","terms":["lipid ROS, iron accumulation, TfR1, NCOA4 ferritinophagy in I/R"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"The levels of iron and MDA content in the reperfused rat hearts were gradually increased with the elongation of reperfusion","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o11","terms":["iron and MDA rise, GPX4 decline in reperfused hearts, cited Tang 2020"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Ferroptosis is an iron-dependent form of necrotic cell death which occurs in myocardial I/R injury (Doll et al., 2019; Ma et al., 2020).","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o12","terms":["ferroptosis as I/R injury mechanism, cited Doll 2019 and Ma 2020"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Our results showed that baicalin greatly improved the cell viability of H9c2 cells after OGD/R exposure","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o13","terms":["H9c2 viability under OGD/R with baicalin"]},{"doc_id":"d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de","exact_quote":"Baicalin blocked all these adverse effects and mitigated the damages resulted from myocardial I/R surgery or OGD/R","kind":"observe","local_id":"t28_o14","terms":["baicalin blocks ROS, lipid peroxidation and iron effects in I/R and OGD/R"]},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o1","t28_o7","t28_o13"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c1","object":"myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury","predicate":"reported to protect against","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to protect against myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury, shown in I/R rats (infarct, ST elevation, function) and H9c2 cells under OGD/R. The section gives no dates."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c2","object":"PI3K/AKT/eNOS pathway in cardiac microvascular endothelial cells","predicate":"reported to act via","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin's cardioprotection in I/R is reported to be mediated by the PI3K/AKT/eNOS pathway in cardiac microvascular endothelial cells, citing Bai et al. 2019."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o3"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c3","object":"inhibition of mitochondrial damage-mediated apoptosis","predicate":"reported to limit infarct via","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin's infarct-limiting effect in myocardial I/R is reported to be associated with inhibition of mitochondrial damage-mediated apoptosis, citing Wang et al. 2013."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o5","t28_o8"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c5","object":"myocardial I/R-triggered and OGD/R-induced ferroptosis","predicate":"reported to suppress","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"The authors' preliminary study suggests baicalin suppresses myocardial I/R-triggered ferroptosis; the main study reports attenuated OGD/R-induced ferroptosis with baicalin treatment."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o10","t28_o14"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c6","object":"lipid ROS, iron accumulation, TfR1 and NCOA4-mediated ferritinophagy in I/R","predicate":"reported to block","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to block I/R- and OGD/R-induced lipid ROS, iron accumulation, TfR1 signaling and NCOA4-mediated ferritinophagy, placing ferroptosis as its protective mechanism."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c7","object":"baicalin-mediated protection in cardiomyocytes (overexpression)","predicate":"reported to abolish","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"ACSL4 overexpression is reported to block baicalin's protective effects in cardiomyocytes. The section does not describe ACSL4's own mechanism in I/R."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o9"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c8","object":"infarct size and left ventricular systolic function after myocardial infarction","predicate":"reported to improve","stance":"reported","subject":"ferrostatin-1","text":"Ferrostatin-1, a ferroptosis inhibitor, is reported to improve infarct size and left ventricular systolic function after myocardial infarction, citing Li W. et al. 2019."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["t28_o12","t28_o11"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t28_c9","object":"myocardial I/R injury","predicate":"reported to occur in and drive","stance":"reported","subject":"ferroptosis","text":"Ferroptosis is reported to occur in myocardial I/R injury and to be critical to it: reperfused rat hearts show rising iron and MDA with falling GPX4, citing Tang 2020."},{"based_on":["t28_o6","t28_o5"],"falsifier":"ACSL4 knockdown or overexpression leaves baicalin's protection and its ferroptosis markers (lipid ROS, iron, GPX4) unchanged in OGD/R cells.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t28_h1","text":"ACSL4 is required for baicalin's anti-ferroptotic protection in cardiomyocytes, so ACSL4 activity links baicalin to ferroptosis suppression in I/R."},{"based_on":["t28_o2","t28_o4","t28_o5"],"falsifier":"A PI3K/AKT inhibitor leaves baicalin's reduction of ferroptosis markers intact in I/R or OGD/R models.","kind":"hypothesis","local_id":"t28_h2","text":"Baicalin's anti-ferroptotic effect in I/R is downstream of or parallel to PI3K/AKT activation, so PI3K/AKT inhibition would weaken it."}],"scope":{"docs":["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de"],"ranges":[["d_d3012628a98d2640b2879ff1df9f2bab1168f0be34e343dfd4ccefc2574e08de",26522,31505]],"topic":null}},"engine_root":"162d8164db6bebc46b7f9a20bb62215ea517c258734edc5cc6cc86638c08de48","outcome":{"kind":"records","result":{"accepted":[