,"ee97cf391651333359154686eb4e578a63138421836c41256625eda0740601cf","f02e5513210d142bf8e658de5ba36400f5c7fa5300b7ac54b719f585d83258f5","f03a6139b3525a6945b89adcbff55880406ca8782e5a706128731a75e0be0246","f1e4bce51306f4b41a477bde35157294f7f7f20b28ee013f308292a9e881043d","f20bea357cb4181107abbec9ad3824f727bc5b50a61ad44c357525cdf154c970","f26edbe912150175b145d9f3b5f6522af80efca944f720e11a71e15cd1fcfc20","f29090ed8edc069d5b136aa46d2424ef381cb80ecfae5d16acdde94f6549766e","f418f54b92afd7e09e79b66b8f68454462621e1d13d2f503152e37a643f0c10c","f4ad7883b815d9c2835b7c23b28452ced95c88dbfc9496327e3cf64582d2aa8a","f57e222904b858f9962e97bd75dd51a7c905aeb1f1537dd5ca8e4628c680ed79","f7b3d426ab07b3396f5b464435005685bcb31de55b2d815e228ac048fc923a08","fab33466d3c0cbf7b5504f5d84ce95a126feed53a1a6e9eb8648ac6415102179","fbabd6969f766c63fb51c0167befc532aef347fe38458c8753dc3fb6f9815ca2","fe3f942c9867e06faf43b6db4114e56bad32c3709618771ac51c1838cb219e61","fef3b2dfb389e7740bb2c4bba10813fc50f2e5a035af420dffa22efbd1fe96c2","ff1789db7bf20acb13d83112fc4f0d7fd5f0ecd2c2758897ab0d8aa5d99043d3","ff200d1979110442f002ae042b4987cfe7f0496c94b87944e14f4dd447efbf84","ff2153beb830c7be3314400833ce9c3b4bc33f73a021fa1d6831c951635c67f4","ff37fdfffc07ba04a88ef215cc70f47de4326233ac8cd81b242a6a59148a2848"],"directive":"TS31-5e47a06f0493932b","kind":"submit","lines":[{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@2d6114847486a247"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c1","object":"PUFA-containing phospholipids, substrates for lipid peroxidation","predicate":"is an essential enzyme that synthesizes","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"ACSL4 is described as an essential enzyme synthesizing PUFA-containing phospholipids, the primary substrates for lipid peroxidation (report dated 2021-04-14)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@4676802df183c105"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c2","object":"ferroptosis","predicate":"is essential for ferroptosis induction; inhibition prevents ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"Cited previous studies indicate ACSL4 is essential for ferroptosis induction and its inhibition prevents ferroptosis; stated as background, not as I/R-specific data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@a12159c82c8ae474"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c3","object":"rat myocardial I/R tissue","predicate":"is upregulated in","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"In the rat myocardial I/R model, ACSL4 expression was dramatically upregulated (I/R 4.411 vs control 1.000), reported in the 2021-04-14 study."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@ad45e9a9a8a9d212"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c4","object":"H9c2 cells in vitro","predicate":"is raised by OGD/R and lowered by baicalin","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL4","text":"In OGD/R-treated H9c2 cells, ACSL4 rose (4.268 vs 1.000); baicalin lowered it dose-dependently (BA-25 2.690, BA-50 2.174, BA-100 1.322), in vitro."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@30fda4b1b4c27f22","@d63ed6cc9e12f057"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c6","object":"ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis resistance (in vitro)","predicate":"concluded to ameliorate I/R injury via","stance":"qualified","subject":"baicalin, ACSL4, ferroptosis","text":"Authors conclude baicalin ameliorates myocardial I/R injury via ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis resistance, but the cited evidence is H9c2 OGD/R in vitro only."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@004b1fd5330dde2b","@c9c9031f9dbf0776"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c7","object":"ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis","predicate":"proposed to prevent I/R injury via suppressing","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Authors propose baicalin prevents myocardial I/R injury by suppressing ACSL4-controlled ferroptosis; the section's in vivo results do not include a direct ACSL4 manipulation."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@be42f51a2af1a8e9","@e48607cc49ff61c8","@962232c8c9d2fe36"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c8","object":"rat myocardial I/R injury","predicate":"reduces infarct size and ST elevation in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In rat LAD I/R with 6-day baicalin pretreatment, infarct size fell to 16.13-21.80% from 34.96% in I/R controls, and ST elevation was reduced."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@1b7c253885dfa4f7","@bd4bcd73e6db302e","@314de317f33b0fdc"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c9","object":"myocardial I/R model rats","predicate":"reported to inhibit ROS production and lipid peroxidation in","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In I/R rats, baicalin (BA-100, BA-200) reduced ROS and lipid peroxidation and raised SOD and GPX4; these are marker-level readouts, not a direct ACSL4 test."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@0adc4dac926a0d37","@240331d308367a2f","@3873a9a20ee26bfb","@f26edbe912150175","@0697569dd74b6ea2","@2bf0420973a898f7","@aedf6a7dfe8871fd"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c10","object":"OGD/R-challenged H9c2 cells","predicate":"reported to attenuate ROS and lipid peroxidation and improve viability of","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"In OGD/R H9c2 cells, baicalin raised viability (58.13% to 86.42%), lowered ROS and MDA, and restored SOD and GPX4 in a dose-related pattern, in vitro only."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@62422b673c5d20a1","@a3d89253376ea405"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c11","object":"lipid peroxidation, iron, TfR1, NCOA4 ferritinophagy","predicate":"reported to be enhanced and reversed by baicalin","stance":"reported","subject":"ferroptosis-related markers","text":"Lipid peroxidation, iron accumulation, TfR1 and NCOA4-mediated ferritinophagy are reported enhanced in I/R and OGD/R models, and reversed by baicalin."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@dd576f6594365598","@0f42c1dbaa798004","@21a1185ee5d7dfe9","@e5880998f70fdc57"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c12","object":"ferroptosis resistance","predicate":"is not known to protect against I/R via","stance":"open","subject":"baicalin","text":"Whether baicalin protects via ferroptosis resistance is stated as not understood; the 2021-04-14 study aims to test it in rat I/R and H9c2 OGD/R, with ferroptosis results not shown."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@9a59d3d135bfe10f"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c13","object":"anti-fibrotic effect","predicate":"decreases ACSL4 expression, leading to","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin is reported to decrease ACSL4 expression, producing an anti-fibrotic effect (Wu et al., 2018); the tissue context of this fibrosis finding is not stated."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@b602d4ade9efbfd7","@800dce0abe70d859","@6e41a435d946b5ea"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c15","object":"myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury","predicate":"is implicated in; blocking it protects","stance":"reported","subject":"ferroptosis","text":"Ferroptosis is implicated in myocardial I/R injury (Park 2019); ferroptosis inhibitors alleviate ischemic organ injury; blocking ferroptosis protects myocardial cells (review 2021-10-23)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@0002b0370ce45e3f"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c16","object":"myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury","predicate":"can trigger","stance":"reported","subject":"PCI reperfusion","text":"Reperfusion after PCI in acute MI can trigger I/R injury with cell death and cardiac dysfunction (Liang et al., 2017), as stated in the 2021-04-14 study."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@690cdb063c75ce35","@94996c9f1ad97dac","@a202f57849d18296","@4495a54f3a0269bf"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c17","object":"isolated perfused hearts; MIRI cardioprotection","predicate":"reported to prevent IRI; mechanism not stated as ferroptosis inhibition","stance":"qualified","subject":"deferoxamine","text":"Deferoxamine, an iron chelator, prevents isolated perfused hearts from IRI in vitro and reduces radical production in CABG; the review does not state ferroptosis inhibition as the mechanism."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@f03a6139b3525a69"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c18","object":"ERS, ROS, GPX-4, autophagy-dependent ferroptosis","predicate":"mainly focus on, with ACSL4 not named among","stance":"open","subject":"ferroptosis studies in MIRI","text":"The 2021-10-23 review names ERS, ROS production, GPX-4 and autophagy-dependent ferroptosis as MIRI focus areas; ACSL4 is not named, and no ACSL4 role in MIRI is given."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@f20bea357cb41811","@62df9f59f7fc0f7b"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c19","object":"breast cancer cells; PUFA-PE formation","predicate":"reported to suppress ferroptosis when knocked down; catalyzes acylation of PUFA to PUFA-CoA","stance":"reported","subject":"ACSL-4","text":"Knockdown of ACSL-4 in breast cancer cells reduces PUFA-PE and suppresses ferroptosis; ACSL-4 acylates PUFA to PUFA-CoA upstream of PUFA-PE (cited, non-cardiac context)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@7f5c67aec04f0048","@788f24f6a0cfe92f"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c20","object":"ferroptosis onset","predicate":"reported to specifically inhibit ACSL-4 and suppress ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"thiazolidinediones; ACSL-4 and LOX","text":"Thiazolidinediones are reported to specifically inhibit ACSL-4 and suppress ferroptosis; decreasing ACSL-4 and LOX suppresses PUFA-PE action. No cardiac or ischemia data are given."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@f20bea357cb41811","@933f8139a2eae6c6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c21","object":"cardiac I/R ferroptosis inhibition by ACSL-4","predicate":"does not establish","stance":"open","subject":"ACSL-4 in the review","text":"The 2021-10-23 review gives no myocardial I/R, cardioprotection or baicalin data for ACSL-4; its ferroptosis examples are from breast cancer and HT22 neuronal cells."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@7b692fb8e7e04381","@a346fec8577d9ca1"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c22","object":"mechanism of MIRI","predicate":"may be involved in","stance":"open","subject":"VDAC pathway and mPTP","text":"VDAC pathway and mPTP may be involved in the MIRI mechanism, with mitochondria as key targets; hedged, and no cardiac experimental data are given in the review."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@8cf228b81c5a4376","@dcc640a6aeba00c7","@21f011f484d4961e"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c23","object":"HT-1080 cells","predicate":"modulate sensitivity to erastin-induced ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"SLC7A11; VDAC-2 and VDAC-3","text":"In HT-1080 cells, SLC7A11 silencing raised erastin-induced ferroptosis sensitivity; VDAC-2/3 knockdown conferred tolerance. Cell-line evidence only, not cardiac."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@609ef2940385f10d","@056d3083644ca6d2"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c24","object":"ferroptosis","predicate":"will promote ROS and lipid peroxidation; will ultimately lead to ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"GPX-4 inhibition; System Xc- inhibition","text":"GPX-4 inhibition promotes ROS and lipid peroxidation leading to ferroptosis; System Xc- inhibition lowers GSH and GPX-4 activity, ultimately causing ferroptosis (citing ref 30)."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@a26048982385d478","@204a148f6b846b8c","@ca3b3cf067ac1f70"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c25","object":"ferroptosis","predicate":"reported to suppress or promote ferroptosis via iron handling","stance":"reported","subject":"HSPB-1, IREB-2, HO-1","text":"HSPB-1 inhibits TFR-1 to lower iron and suppress ferroptosis; IREB-2 limits iron uptake; HO-1 promotes ferroptosis via iron increase and lipid peroxidation. No injury models given."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@933f8139a2eae6c6"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c26","object":"HT22 neuronal cells","predicate":"reported to inhibit erastin and ferroptosis in","stance":"reported","subject":"zileuton","text":"Zileuton (5-LOX inhibitor) reportedly inhibits erastin-induced ferroptosis in HT22 neuronal cells; this is neuronal, not cardiac, and is not a cardioprotection finding."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@596cd28c4a1ae3ef","@1ae31b5f538c3065","@6338843ef3991089"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c27","object":"rat MIRI and cardiomyocytes","predicate":"probably increases ERS, which increases ferroptosis; reported to form a vicious circle","stance":"reported","subject":"erastin; ERS; ferroptosis","text":"Erastin may increase ERS in a rat MIRI model, further increasing ferroptosis; ERS inhibition alleviates ferroptosis and MIRI, and ferroptosis and ERS form a vicious circle."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@a84d55033565fe37","@042477e4eabc27b0"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c28","object":"diabetic rat MIRI model","predicate":"reported to attenuate ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes in","stance":"reported","subject":"ferrostatin-1; salubrinal","text":"In a diabetic rat LAD MIRI model, ferrostatin-1 and the ERS inhibitor salubrinal are each reported to attenuate ERS-induced ferroptosis in cardiomyocytes."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@fbabd6969f766c63","@756d27a735214c6f","@c8d47a74b00b7778"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c29","object":"GPX-4 and ROS; cardiomyocytes in MIRI","predicate":"reported to inhibit ferroptosis and alleviate MIRI; reported to improve ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"liproxstatin-1; SIRT-1","text":"Liproxstatin-1 reportedly inhibits ferroptosis and alleviates MIRI by raising GPX-4 and reducing lipid-peroxidation ROS; SIRT-1 overexpression improves cardiomyocyte ferroptosis."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@ee97cf3916513333","@0c65c331cddca620","@c8e601aa604ff06b"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c30","object":"mouse IRI model; cardiomyocytes","predicate":"accumulates at scar; reported as predictive biomarker and direct evidence of ferroptosis","stance":"reported","subject":"ferritin; PEox; GCIB-SIMS","text":"Ferritin accumulates in mouse myocardial scar 30 min after LAD ligation in an IRI model; PEox is a predictive ferroptosis biomarker and GCIB-SIMS gives direct evidence in cardiomyocytes."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@c9088c8a7d65820b"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c31","object":"vitiligo skin lesions","predicate":"reported to achieve repigmentation via anti-inflammatory effects","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"Baicalin in the 2021-11-11 vitiligo review repigments vitiligo lesions via anti-inflammatory and JAK/STAT effects; that report has no cardiac, I/R or ferroptosis data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@7b7f688f79cb87ea"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c32","object":"antioxidant, immunity, lipid metabolism, anti-inflammatory","predicate":"reported to have pharmacological activities including","stance":"reported","subject":"baicalin","text":"The 2021-11-11 vitiligo review lists baicalin as antioxidant, immunoregulatory, lipid-regulating and anti-inflammatory (Xin 2020) with no cardiac injury data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@0f9f7b36fcf32e77","@041a74effc9827ef","@5610f6c9b70e64ce","@de8ed09d3eca8066","@20a2568a54c07ed5","@97e440f1198df149"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c33","object":"cardioprotection or ferroptosis inhibition","predicate":"listed generally or in melanocyte models","stance":"qualified","subject":"other natural compounds in vitiligo review","text":"The 2021-11-11 vitiligo review lists kaempferol, paeoniflorin, puerarin, EGCG, paeonol and morin only generally or in melanocyte models; no heart ferroptosis or ACSL4 data."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@041a74effc9827ef"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c34","object":"ferroptosis inhibition or ACSL4 role in myocardial I/R","predicate":"does not establish","stance":"open","subject":"paeoniflorin cardioprotection","text":"The paeoniflorin cardioprotection statement in the vitiligo review gives no I/R, ferroptosis or ACSL4 data, so it does not establish ferroptosis inhibition in the heart."},{"as_of":null,"based_on":["@17c75288b243c946","@b605a632919b75c6","@ca23abe17b9e48cb","@7b7f688f79cb87ea"],"kind":"claim","local_id":"t31_c35","object":"baicalin, CBD, 1,5-dicQA, THSG and others","predicate":"are general claims without cardiac ferroptosis or ACSL4 data","stance":"qualified","subject":"vitiligo review compound listings","text":"Natural-compound listings in the vitiligo review (2021-11-11), including baicalin and CBD, are general 